nodes.directive:
Read the complete originating request and `{{workspace_path}}/task.md`. The current canonical values supplied by the workflow are:

- task_description: {{task_description}}
- expected_result: {{expected_result}}

Verify that task.md exactly projects those values. Create one complete ordered plan of 1..100 meaningful items. Each item has one stable ID, one actionable unit, and a concrete observable expected result; every ID must be pairwise unique across the whole array even when two items otherwise differ. Cover the whole task without inventing authority or imposing universal commits, tests, publication, deployment, or named tools when they are not required by the task.

Write `{{workspace_path}}/plan.json` as exactly the returned `steps` array encoded as JSON; it is the durable projection, not a second plan. Verify ID uniqueness over the complete array, then return only `steps`. Do not execute any item. If the complete plan, unique identity, and exact projection cannot be verified, report the blocker and do not submit.
